# Copy to .env.local and adjust. Everything here is optional: the build scripts
# auto-detect the Visual Studio C++ toolchain, the CLion-bundled Ninja, the
# Visual Studio CMake, and the vcpkg checkout first. Only set a value when
# detection picks the wrong one.

# CMake >= 3.27
# CMAKE=C:\Program Files\Microsoft Visual Studio\18\Community\Common7\IDE\CommonExtensions\Microsoft\CMake\CMake\bin\cmake.exe

# Ninja
# NINJA=E:\Jetbrains\CLion 2026.1.2\bin\ninja\win\x64\ninja.exe

# Visual Studio installation with the C++ build tools (auto-detected via vswhere)
# VSWHERE=C:\Program Files (x86)\Microsoft Visual Studio\Installer\vswhere.exe

# C++ toolchain: "msvc" (default on Windows, static release build) or "mingw".
# The CLion-bundled MinGW 15.2 cannot link -static, so only use it for
# diagnostics; it is not suitable for the release sidecar.
# RT_PN_CXX=msvc

# MinGW-w64 toolchain directory (the directory containing g++.exe), fallback only
# PTPN_MINGW_BIN=E:\Jetbrains\CLion 2026.1.2\bin\mingw\bin

# vcpkg checkout (the directory containing vcpkg.exe and scripts/buildsystems)
# VCPKG_ROOT=D:\vcpkg

# Cargo/rustc shims if the Rust toolchain is not on PATH
# CARGO=cargo
# RUSTC=rustc

# CLion installation root, used to find its bundled CMake/Ninja/MinGW
# CLION_HOME=E:\Jetbrains\CLion 2026.1.2
